  "notes": {
    "addrDesktop": {
      "x": 0,
      "y": -300,
      "text": "Addresses — desktop",
      "kind": "title1",
      "maxW": 4480,
      "page": "addresses"
    },
    "addrPhone": {
      "x": 0,
      "y": 1370,
      "text": "Addresses — phone",
      "kind": "title1",
      "maxW": 1330,
      "page": "addresses"
    },
    "addrNotes": {
      "x": 4560,
      "y": 0,
      "w": 380,
      "maxH": 520,
      "fill": "yellow",
      "page": "addresses",
      "text": "Decisions in this page:\n• Copy is the main action: tap a field to copy it, or Copy all. The clipboard clears after 60 s.\n• Usage Locations become a checklist with progress (\"3 of 5 updated\"); the 7-column table only remains on wide desktop as columns inside each row.\n• Status Current / Old can be changed from the detail page (today it has no control).\n• Delete moves to the detail page's danger zone; the list keeps a row menu.\n• Same pattern is reused by Mobile numbers."
    },
    "mobDesktop": {
      "x": 0,
      "y": -300,
      "text": "Mobile numbers — desktop",
      "kind": "title1",
      "maxW": 2960,
      "page": "mobiles"
    },
    "mobPhone": {
      "x": 0,
      "y": 1220,
      "text": "Mobile numbers — phone",
      "kind": "title1",
      "maxW": 1330,
      "page": "mobiles"
    },
    "mobNotes": {
      "x": 3040,
      "y": 1020,
      "w": 380,
      "maxH": 480,
      "fill": "yellow",
      "page": "mobiles",
      "text": "Decisions in this page:\n• Parity with Addresses: search, counters, empty state with an action, visible delete (no hover-only button).\n• Copy number and a Call action (tel: link) on the detail page.\n• Country code uses the same searchable picker as Addresses.\n• Usage Locations reuse the Address checklist exactly; only the noun changes."
    },
    "subDesktop": {
      "x": 0,
      "y": -300,
      "text": "Subscriptions — desktop",
      "kind": "title1",
      "maxW": 2960,
      "page": "subscriptions"
    },
    "subPhone": {
      "x": 0,
      "y": 1270,
      "text": "Subscriptions — phone",
      "kind": "title1",
      "maxW": 1330,
      "page": "subscriptions"
    },
    "subNotes": {
      "x": 3040,
      "y": 1020,
      "w": 380,
      "maxH": 520,
      "fill": "yellow",
      "page": "subscriptions",
      "text": "Decisions in this page:\n• One headline number: a monthly equivalent across cycles (per currency, plus the converted total when the user asks for it).\n• \"Renews in N days\" replaces a bare date; within 7 days it turns amber.\n• Status is a pill and a filter (Active default); Cancelled and Expired drop out of totals as today.\n• Payment method, renewal type and tier finally show on the detail.\n• Inline field errors on the form; end date available when adding."
    },
    "ytDesktop": {
      "x": 0,
      "y": -300,
      "text": "YouTube — desktop",
      "kind": "title1",
      "maxW": 5960,
      "page": "youtube"
    },
    "ytPhone": {
      "x": 0,
      "y": 2600,
      "text": "YouTube — phone",
      "kind": "title1",
      "maxW": 1330,
      "page": "youtube"
    },
    "ytNotes": {
      "x": 6080,
      "y": 0,
      "w": 380,
      "maxH": 560,
      "fill": "yellow",
      "page": "youtube",
      "text": "Decisions in this page:\n• One page header with tabs Videos / Shorts / Channels, no card-in-card.\n• Sync freshness and the Sync button sit together in the header.\n• Three distinct notices: Connect (first time), Access withdrawn (permanent, explains why and what was deleted), Temporarily unavailable (try later). Today one notice covers all three.\n• Empty directory copy points to Channels, not to a list that isn't there.\n• Weekly digest stays on the Account page; Channels links to it.\nBackend: telling \"withdrawn\" from \"down\" needs the availability check to return a reason.\n• First look (access granted, not connected) uses today's copy word for word: the six storage points, the Before you connect points, the agreement and Connect YouTube. Tweak \"state\" shows ticked, the not-ticked error and the revoked note.\n• Flagged, not changed: connecting imports no channels, so the first connected view says \"No channels yet\"; a failed status or auth-url call shows nothing."
    },
    "vaultDesktop": {
      "x": 0,
      "y": -300,
      "text": "Vault — desktop",
      "kind": "title1",
      "maxW": 9040,
      "page": "vault"
    },
    "vaultPhone": {
      "x": 0,
      "y": 2700,
      "text": "Vault — phone",
      "kind": "title1",
      "maxW": 3680,
      "page": "vault"
    },
    "vaultNotes": {
      "x": 9120,
      "y": 0,
      "w": 380,
      "maxH": 760,
      "fill": "yellow",
      "page": "vault",
      "text": "Decisions in this page:\n• Every section from today's Vault page is here, with its copy kept word for word: Unlock, Change passphrase, Rotate recovery key, Encrypted Escape Copy (Google Drive), Export, Import, the offline reader, Remove local vault.\n• First open while locked: the Unlock panel replaces the status hero. Passphrase and recovery-key cards are disabled with today's reason; backups, export, import and the reader still work.\n• Change passphrase and Rotate recovery key move into dialogs (phone: pushed screens) that carry their full explanations. The cards keep their one-line description.\n• Change passphrase has a tweak for the recovery-key unlock path (\"Set new passphrase\").\n• Import and Restore from Google Drive share one replace dialog; its text and tick box follow what the file changes.\n• Remove dialog: the button says \"Remove from this device\" instead of today's \"Delete\".\n• Sample recovery keys are placeholders, never real keys."
    },
    "accDesktop": {
      "x": 0,
      "y": -300,
      "text": "Account — desktop",
      "kind": "title1",
      "maxW": 4480,
      "page": "account"
    },
    "accPhone": {
      "x": 0,
      "y": 1600,
      "text": "Account — phone",
      "kind": "title1",
      "maxW": 1330,
      "page": "account"
    },
    "accNotes": {
      "x": 4560,
      "y": 0,
      "w": 380,
      "maxH": 600,
      "fill": "yellow",
      "page": "account",
      "text": "Decisions in this page:\n• Wording follows today's Account page; new copy only where today has none (profile header, Preferences line, backup summary).\n• A profile header (today the page has no identity or title).\n• Order: backups summary, Preferences, Weekly YouTube digest (only when YouTube is connected), Install MyOrganiser (hidden once installed), Delete account.\n• The backup summary links to the Vault page instead of duplicating it.\n• Delete keeps today's two steps. Step 1 offers an Escape Copy; its button reads \"Continue without a copy\" until one is downloaded, then \"Continue\" (tweak on the step 1 board). Step 2 asks for the password and DELETE."
    },
    "admDesktop": {
      "x": 0,
      "y": -300,
      "text": "Admin portal — desktop",
      "kind": "title1",
      "maxW": 5960,
      "page": "admin"
    },
    "admPhone": {
      "x": 0,
      "y": 1220,
      "text": "Admin portal — phone",
      "kind": "title1",
      "maxW": 1330,
      "page": "admin"
    },
    "admNotes": {
      "x": 6080,
      "y": 0,
      "w": 380,
      "maxH": 560,
      "fill": "orange",
      "page": "admin",
      "text": "Decisions and backend needs:\n• Users: filter chips (role, status), sort, paging — needs list-users paging and filters.\n• User detail: sectioned cards; actions grouped by risk; you cannot disable or demote yourself (button disabled with a reason).\n• Recent activity on the user page — needs audit log filtered by user.\n• Audit log: names instead of raw ids, action pills, filters, paging past 50 — needs names joined and paging.\n• Every destructive action keeps a confirm dialog that says exactly what happens."
    },
    "adminBackend": {
      "fill": "orange",
      "maxH": 420,
      "page": "dashboard",
      "text": "Backend needed for the admin overview:\n• A stats endpoint: user totals by role, disabled, unverified, YouTube Access places used.\n• Audit log: actor and target names (today raw ids), plus paging past the newest 50.\n• Users list: paging, sort, and role / status filters (today search only).\nEach needs an API change and yarn openapi:sync before the UI can ship.",
      "w": 380,
      "x": 3040,
      "y": 0
    },
