    "fbDesktop": {
      "x": 0,
      "y": -300,
      "text": "Feedback — desktop",
      "kind": "title1",
      "maxW": 6000,
      "page": "feedback"
    },
    "fbPhone": {
      "x": 0,
      "y": 1500,
      "text": "Feedback — phone",
      "kind": "title1",
      "maxW": 1800,
      "page": "feedback"
    },
    "fbNotes": {
      "x": 6080,
      "y": 0,
      "w": 380,
      "maxH": 760,
      "fill": "yellow",
      "page": "feedback",
      "text": "Decisions in this page:\n• Wording is today's, word for word, from the dialog, Your reports, the follow-up form and the unsubscribe page.\n• Entry points: \"Send feedback\" in the sidebar footer and the account menu (desktop), and the More tab (phone). Your reports sits on the Account page with its Updated badge.\n• The dialog keeps the plaintext warning and shows the Report Context before sending. Tweak \"kind\" switches Bug report and Suggestion.\n• Status pills: Received and Under review neutral and blue, Planned violet, Fixed and Shipped teal, Won't do red, Can't reproduce amber outline.\n• The unsubscribe page has a tweak for its four states: working, done, invalid, error.\n• New illustration: feedback (two speech bubbles). Added to Foundations."
    },
    "afDesktop": {
      "x": 0,
      "y": -300,
      "text": "Admin feedback — desktop",
      "kind": "title1",
      "maxW": 4480,
      "page": "adminfeedback"
    },
    "afPhone": {
      "x": 0,
      "y": 1400,
      "text": "Admin feedback — phone",
      "kind": "title1",
      "maxW": 860,
      "page": "adminfeedback"
    },
    "afNotes": {
      "x": 4560,
      "y": 0,
      "w": 380,
      "maxH": 760,
      "fill": "orange",
      "page": "adminfeedback",
      "text": "Decisions and backend needs:\n• Feedback joins the admin sidebar and the admin phone tab bar, with the slate inbox illustration.\n• Sidebar badge counts Received reports — needs a count endpoint (none today).\n• Inbox keeps today's filters (Status, Kind, Platform, Tracking issue). Platform becomes a dropdown (Any platform, Web, iOS, Android) instead of free text — the column is a plain string today, so the backend should validate these three values and columns; adds paging (Newer / Older) — needs offset or cursor paging (today: first 100, no paging).\n• Report detail splits the reading column from a Triage panel, so every action sits beside what it acts on. All wording is today's.\n• Triage keeps inline messages, no toasts or confirm dialogs, as today.\n• Fixed and Shipped show only the final note, the Tracking Issue and Reopen.\n• Admin Home is still a redirect today; the v2 Overview replaces it."
    },
    "lgDesktop": {
      "x": 0,
      "y": -300,
      "text": "Legal pages — desktop",
      "kind": "title1",
      "maxW": 4480,
      "page": "legal"
    },
    "lgPhone": {
      "x": 0,
      "y": 3400,
      "text": "Legal pages — phone",
      "kind": "title1",
      "maxW": 1330,
      "page": "legal"
    },
    "lgNotes": {
      "x": 4560,
      "y": 0,
      "w": 380,
      "maxH": 900,
      "fill": "yellow",
      "page": "legal",
      "text": "Decisions in this page:\n• Every word of Privacy, Terms and How we store your YouTube data is today's, unchanged. Only the layout is new.\n• One public layout for all three: a slim header with Privacy Policy and Terms of Service, a navy title band with an illustration, an On this page list, numbered section cards, and the landing footer line.\n• On the phone the On this page list sits above the text.\n• The same section components still feed the Sign up dialog (h3 there).\n• Operator & Contact shows placeholder values; the real ones come from OPERATOR_NAME and OPERATOR_CONTACT_EMAIL.\n• Flagged, not changed: Terms has no Last updated line; How we store your YouTube data links only to /dashboard/youtube, so a signed-out reader has no way back. There is no separate YouTube terms page — Terms links to YouTube's own."
    }
